/**
 * THE SIX INVITE FLOWS — the first handoff written in this folder, as the
 * practice run of `/dev-handoff-notes` with its designer (2026-10-27). Four
 * that morning; the verified-email and signed-in journeys joined the same
 * afternoon.
 *
 * One build, six journeys picked from the Invite flow design control. Every
 * screen decides what to draw by asking two questions — who sent the learner
 * (a partner, or nobody) and what that carried (their email, or nothing) —
 * never by comparing to a flow by name. The components below were the thirteen
 * SCREENS until 2026-11-01, when Jillienne folded them into the five things a
 * developer actually builds — "there should not be that many cards": what the
 * learner sees off-site, the public site, the invited product page, the
 * checkout with its two modals, and the confirmation with its endings and
 * holds. Nothing was dropped in the fold; a screen that became part of a card
 * is a named variant of it, and Checkout's 32 variants were trimmed to the
 * sixteen a developer reads as distinct.
 */
